Code that runs on after a throw elsewhere reads a cell (a fiber parked inside `Task.uninterruptible`, `uninterruptibleMask` or a helper over it; a fiber under `Task.withScheduler`; the frame parked in a mask; a function hosting a writer that a caller masks; a detached reader while the frame writes under another scheduler), and each update writes a copy of the contents, accepted (ownership-v3-kernel.md §13 item 12, *A defect*, (d), #2613). Its live twin is CellRunsOnLive.
